
This directory contains some simple examples of planning domains
and planning problems, written in PDDL.

Test these domains at http://editor.planning.domains/ or with one of the other
planners I've mentioned in class (FF or Fast Downward).

domain1.pddl / problem1.pddl
An example of a logistics-style planning problem where different types of vehicles
need to move around packages to particular locations.
[Works with editor.planning.domains]

domain2.pddl / problem2.pddl
Another example of logistics, this time using types.
[Works with editor.planning.domains]

domain3.pddl / problem3.pddl
Another example of logistics, this time using a type hierarchy.
[Does not work with editor.planning.domains but works with FF]

domain4.pddl / problem4.pddl
A logistics example using conditional and quantified effects.
[Does not work with editor.planning.domains but works with FF]

domain5.pddl / problem5.pddl
A logistics example using conditional, quantified effects, and typing.
[Works with editor.planning.domains]*

*There appears to be a bug in editor.planning.domains involving quantified
conditional effects. The example in domain5.pddl presents a workaround by using a
typed variable on "forall". You should compare domain4.pddl and domain5.pddl to see
the difference.

